diagnosis_text:
Every diagnostic layer was checked and all are clean for the pc1-to-pc2 path. Phase 1 reachability probing shows pc2→pc1 at 0% loss with 3.15 ms RTT, directly contradicting the user's report that "nothing answers." Phase A infrastructure sweep (infra_sweep + l2_snapshot) found no ACL drop rules affecting intra-Office-A traffic — the only iptables DROP rules on dswa1 and dswa2 target Office A→Office B cross-site forwarding (10.1.0.0/24→10.3.0.0/24), not traffic within 10.1.0.0/24. Both pc1 and pc2 have each other's MAC addresses in ARP as REACHABLE, confirming L2 visibility. Phase B found the OSPF fabric fully healthy with all expected Full adjacencies, and the TC snapshot shows no shaping, policing, or non-default qdisc on any interface. Phase D found no resource pressure on any device. No flap script, no carrier anomalies, and no mechanism that could cause the reported isolation was found anywhere in the topology. The user's description of "yesterday working, today silent" is consistent with a transient event (brief cable/switch reboot, a momentary software restart) that has since self-cleared, or with misidentification of the peer host. Current live measurements confirm full bidirectional reachability between pc1 (10.1.0.100) and pc2 (10.1.0.101). No fault is present in this network.
=== END ===